# Launcher scripts must keep the line endings their operating system expects,
# whatever the person's git settings are and whether they cloned or downloaded
# the zip. A .bat saved with LF lines misbehaves on Windows; a .sh or .command
# saved with CRLF fails on macOS and Linux ("bad interpreter", "^M"). The CI
# smoke test (scripts/ci_smoke.py) checks these on every operating system.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf
